The amplitude and mean position are
$\begin{aligned}A&=\frac{5.2-0.8}{2}\\&=2.2\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}c&=\frac{5.2+0.8}{2}\\&=3\end{aligned}$
Low tide to the next high tide takes $6.25$ hours, which is half a period.
$\begin{aligned}T&=2(6.25)\\&=12.5\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}a&=\frac{2\pi}{12.5}\\&=\frac{4\pi}{25}\end{aligned}$
The depth starts at its minimum, so $k=-2.2$.
$h(t)=-2.2\cos\left(\frac{4\pi t}{25}\right)+3$.
The sketch confirms low tide at midnight and high tide $6.25$ hours later.
