The amplitude and mean position are
$\begin{aligned}A&=\frac{180-(-180)}{2}\\&=180\end{aligned}$
$c=\frac{180+(-180)}{2}=0$.
A frequency of $40$ cycles per second gives
$T=\frac{1}{40}\text{ s}$.
$\begin{aligned}a&=\frac{2\pi}{1/40}\\&=80\pi\end{aligned}$
The voltage starts at the mean position and rises, so use sine with $k=180$.
$V(t)=180\sin(80\pi t)$.
The sketch shows one cycle, starting at zero and rising.
